    <table cellpadding="0" cellspacing="0" border="0" width="100%">
    <tr>
        <td id="descriptionArea">
            <p><b>Steps to Reproduce:</b></p>
<ul>
	<li>Go to Voicemail app</li>
	<li>Create and activate a Greeting, assign it to a specific recipient/contact, ensure it's within the configured time/day schedule.</li>
	<li>Have that contact call the test device.</li>
	<li>Let the call go unanswered for the configured delay so the greeting should trigger.</li>
	<li>Observe <b>where the greeting audio is actually heard</b> </li>
</ul>


<p> </p>

<p><b>Expected Result:</b> The greeting audio should be routed <b>into the call itself</b>, so the <b>caller</b> (the person who dialed in) hears the greeting message on their end </p>

<p><b>Actual Result:</b> The greeting audio plays out loud on the recipient's own device speaker, not through the call to the caller. The caller (assigned contact) does not hear the greeting at all on their end.</p>
            <br/>
        </td>
    </tr>
    </table>

