    <table cellpadding="2" cellspacing="0" border="0" width="100%" align="center">
    <tr>
        <td bgcolor="#bbbbbb" width="1%" nowrap align="center">
            &nbsp;<font color="#ffffff"><b>Description</b></font>&nbsp;
        </td>
        <td>&nbsp;</td>
    </tr>
    </table>

    <table cellpadding="0" cellspacing="0" border="0" width="100%">
    <tr>
        <td id="descriptionArea">
            <p><b>Steps :</b></p>
<ol>
	<li>Go to Voicemail App.</li>
	<li>Create <b>12 greetings</b> (record audio + title for each, minimal config is fine).</li>
	<li>On the Greetings list screen, toggle several greetings <b>ON</b>.</li>
	<li>Scroll the list down, then back up.</li>
	<li>Observe the toggle states of the greetings you just set.</li>
	<li>Repeat: toggle several greetings <b>OFF</b>, scroll down and up again, and observe.</li>
</ol>


<p><b>Expected Result:</b> Each greeting's toggle should reliably reflect its actual saved state (ON stays ON, OFF stays OFF) regardless of scrolling.</p>

<p><b>Actual Result:</b> After scrolling, some greetings' toggles show an incorrect state — a greeting that was turned ON sometimes appears OFF (or vice versa), and in some cases a greeting gets "stuck" showing ON even after being explicitly turned OFF.</p>
            <br/>
        </td>
    </tr>
    </table>

