    <table cellpadding="2" cellspacing="0" border="0" width="100%" align="center">
    <tr>
        <td bgcolor="#bbbbbb" width="1%" nowrap align="center">
            &nbsp;<font color="#ffffff"><b>Description</b></font>&nbsp;
        </td>
        <td>&nbsp;</td>
    </tr>
    </table>

    <table cellpadding="0" cellspacing="0" border="0" width="100%">
    <tr>
        <td id="descriptionArea">
            <p><b>Steps</b>:</p>
<ul>
	<li>go to Voicemail App</li>
	<li>Select the Create New Greeting button</li>
	<li>Create a Greeting, record audio, set a Title.</li>
	<li>Assign a specific contact/phone number to it (via Select Recipients).</li>
	<li>Set Time (From/To) and Repeat (days) to include the <b>current</b> time/day.</li>
	<li>Set the Greeting's individual toggle to <b>ON</b>.</li>
	<li>Confirm the master Voicemail service toggle (Settings) is <b>ON</b>.</li>
	<li>From the assigned phone number, call the test device and <b>let it go unanswered</b> (don't pick up).</li>
</ul>


<p><b>Expected result</b> : The recorded greeting audio should play to the caller once the call goes unanswered, since the contact, time, and day all match the configured conditions.</p>

<p><b>Actual result</b> : The greeting does not play — caller does not hear the recorded message.</p>
            <br/>
        </td>
    </tr>
    </table>

